                <pb facs="0699" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/1255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-23T18:00:00-04:00">September 23, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. My telegram No. 220, September 16, 4 p.m. and Department’s telegram No. 162,
                    September 19, 4 p.m. Pessimistic observations of some Chilean officials to
                    Commercial Attaché<anchor n="31" xml:id="d819-f1"/> apparently due to the
                    failure of Chilean representatives in Washington to keep them properly informed.
                    They are gratified at bank’s prompt action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
